From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: add minimal PPE multicast replication

A multicast flow never reached an offloaded entry: its destination is a
multicast MAC, and the unicast is_valid_ether_addr() check rejected it
before the entry was built.  The IB2.MULTICAST branch that exists in
prepare was therefore dead code.  Even if it were reached, the entry kept
the single destination port computed for the redirect action, so only one
bridge member would have received the stream.

Accept a multicast destination only when the redirect target is a DSA
user port and at least two switch-facing members of its bridge can be
replicated.  Replication uses the DSA/switch destination bitmap in the L2
etype word that the unicast path already writes as BIT(dsa_port), now
with every member port set.  The force-QoS bit the LAN entries already
carry selects the QDMA1 hardware path behind that word, and multicast
entries are kept off the SRAM fast path as the vendor SDK does.
IB2.MULTICAST stays set so the CPU also gets a copy for any member that
is not behind the switch (WLAN).  Flows that cannot be replicated that
way are refused, leaving the full fan-out to software; this includes
bridges with fewer than two switch-facing members.

The vendor SDK also defines PPE2_MCAST_PPSE (FE + 0x284), but on AN7581
that address reads back as 0xdeadbeef and the SDK never writes it.  This
change does not write it, because the issue forbids writing unknown
registers.  /sys/kernel/debug/ppe/mcast prints the raw register once per
PPE and lists every bound multicast entry with its PSE port, switch port
mask, NBQ/channel and L2 etype.

Only multicast flows are affected; unicast entries keep every field they
had before.  Table geometry, BND_AGE, PPPoE, L2B and the QoS groups are
untouched.  The switch bitmap semantics are taken from the vendor SDK and
are not measured on hardware here.

Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
